WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.080
Priya: Despite the access bottleneck, let's name what worked.

2
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:07.968
Lukas: The team refused promotion without verified fencing.

3
00:00:07.968 --> 00:00:11.232
Raj: We chose to dry-run it first beforehand.

4
00:00:11.232 --> 00:00:14.952
Hannah: That caught the wrong target host identifier.

5
00:00:14.952 --> 00:00:18.576
Anika: Our smoke test checked actual order retrieval.

6
00:00:18.576 --> 00:00:22.464
Priya: Just to confirm, safety checks stay, right?

7
00:00:22.464 --> 00:00:26.880
Lukas: Let me play that back. Faster isn't always better.

8
00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:31.968
Raj: Exactly. We can shorten approval waits, not fencing.

9
00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:37.728
Hannah: Maybe automate evidence collection without removing independent checks.

10
00:00:37.728 --> 00:00:42.480
Priya: Good distinction. Keep the successful steps visible.

